  timer: 0
  sprite: stalker_slash
  anchor: center
  narration: "It opens up at you in a quick raking strike."
  > deal_damage 1d4

+move ambush
  intent: heavy_attack
  preview: "It pulls back into the reeds. The patterns bleed into the dark."
  timer: 3
  sprite: stalker_ambush
  anchor: bottom
  narration: "It comes back out of cover at a longer angle than you'd expect, and lands."
  > deal_damage 2d8
  > inflict_condition poisoned dc 12 33%

+intro
It has been watching you for some time. You realize this in the
half-second before it comes out of the reeds — too low in the hip, too
long in the shoulder, the wet skin patterned like nothing that ever
lived. It does not roar. It does not posture. It crosses the open water
between you in a single coiled stride and is on its second when you raise
your weapon.

+win
> +give_gold 10
> +add_tag killed_bog_stalker
The patterns across the wet skin slow, settle, and stop. The carcass
sinks where it lies, the open water taking it back the way the open
water takes most things on the deep paths.

+lose
> +damage_spirits 100
